hi we know that in specific antigen  there are small portions of the antigen  for example here marked in blue which is  going to be recognized by the antibody  whether its membrane bound b-cell  receptor or a secreted antibody and this  small portion in the large protein is  known as the epitope now inside the  whole protein there could be multiple  different epitope right and sometimes  one epitope could be selectively  detected by one class of antibodies and  that class of antibodies might not  detect any other epitope shown here so  that category of antibody could be  termed as monoclonal antibody now other  antibodies which are going to detect  many of these epitope at least few of  these epitope non-specifically they're  termed as polyclonal antibody and in  other video we would look at how  monoclonal antibody is generated  artificially now another important term  which is confusing or sometimes people  misunderstand that is per octave so  epitope is a part of the antigen a small  part of the antigen which is going to be  presented to the t-cell receptor or the  P cell receptor that is the epitope of  an antigen but a para top is that part  of the antibody which is interacting  with the epitope so definitely para tope  resides in the variable region of the  antibody the variable region pericope  consists of the hyper variable loop loop  which is going to directly interact with  the epitope so that's how we just kind  of explain the terminologies of epitope  and para tube in this video for short  video thank you if you like my video  even a thumbs up don't forget to Like  share and subscribe thank you
 

